{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" --help\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" probes --help\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" fresh-rerun --help'","aggregated_output":"usage: assessment.py [-h] {check,probes,response,validate,fresh-rerun} ...\n\nRun the pinned assessment helpers in their recorded Pixi environment.\n\npositional arguments:\n  {check,probes,response,validate,fresh-rerun}\n  arguments\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: run_probes.py [-h] [-o OUTPUT] [--response RESPONSE]\n                     [--only {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]]\n                     [--skip {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]]\n                     [--check-remote] [--allow GLOB [GLOB ...]]\n                     [--kind {dataset,component,study,skill}] [--overwrite]\n                     [--quiet]\n                     path\n\nRun the STAMPED probes over a checked-out research object.\n\n    run_probes.py <path> [-o probes.json] [--response response.json]\n                  [--only NAME ...] [--skip NAME ...] [--check-remote]\n                  [--kind dataset|component|study|skill]\n\nWrites the per-probe results, and optionally a response JSON (the format in\n``../stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md``) in which every item a\nprobe speaks to carries that probe's verdict and every other item is left\n``not-checked`` for the assessing session to judge.\n\nThe probes never modify the object.  Nothing here replaces the judgement items:\na response straight out of this script is a draft, not an assessment.\n\npositional arguments:\n  path                  checked-out object to probe\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  -o, --output OUTPUT   write the probe results here\n  --response RESPONSE   also write a draft response JSON here\n  --only {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]\n                        run just these probes\n  --skip {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]\n  --check-remote        contact submodule urls (network)\n  --allow GLOB [GLOB ...]\n                        paths no-abs-paths may skip, for files that genuinely\n                        have to carry a host path\n  --kind {dataset,component,study,skill}\n  --overwrite           replace an existing --response file instead of keeping\n                        its judged answers\n  --quiet\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: fresh_rerun.py [-h] (--url URL | --path PATH) [--entry ENTRY]\n                      [--outputs OUTPUTS [OUTPUTS ...]]\n                      [--in-container CONTAINER] [--rtol RTOL]\n                      [--workdir WORKDIR] [--timeout TIMEOUT] [--keep-outputs]\n                      [--max-get-gb MAX_GET_GB] [-o OUTPUT]\n\nThe `fresh-rerun` probe: clone the published object elsewhere and re-run it.\n\nThis probe tests re-creation in a fresh clone. Running it on the original host\ndoes not establish portability to another host; the report records the host.\n\n    fresh_rerun.py --url <published url> [--entry 'make all'] [--in-container IMAGE]\n                   [--outputs 'results/*.tsv' 'figures/*.png'] [--rtol 1e-6]\n                   [--workdir DIR] [-o fresh-rerun.json]\n\nIt never touches the original object: everything happens in a temporary clone\n(kept under --workdir when given, so the evidence survives the probe).\n\nSteps\n-----\n1. clone from the published location (``datalad clone`` when available, else\n   ``git clone``) — a clone that fails is already D.1 ``unmet``;\n2. install the modules without content (``datalad get -n -r``) and fetch only\n   what fits under ``--max-get-gb``: an unbounded ``datalad get -r .`` started\n   on the **3.7 TiB** a module of ``///repronim/containers`` makes reachable —\n   87 GB of it had landed before anyone noticed — because that module carries\n   every image the registry knows. The entry point fetches its own declared\n   inputs;\n3. record the checksums the clone *shipped* for the output files, then **remove\n   them**, so that only re-creation counts (``--keep-outputs`` to opt out);\n4. run the entry point, in a container when ``--in-container`` is given;\n5. compare: identical checksums, or numeric agreement within ``--rtol`` for\n   tables, and report anything else as a difference for a human to look at.\n\nExit code 0 means the probe ran, not that the object reproduced; read\n``status`` in the JSON.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --url URL             published location to clone from (what D.1 promises)\n  --path PATH           local path to clone from (indicative only: does not\n                        test D.1)\n  --entry ENTRY         command to run (default: datalad rerun, else make)\n  --outputs OUTPUTS [OUTPUTS ...]\n                        glob(s) naming the outputs to compare\n  --in-container CONTAINER\n                        apptainer/singularity image to run --entry inside\n  --rtol RTOL           relative tolerance for tables\n  --workdir WORKDIR     keep the clone here instead of a temp dir\n  --timeout TIMEOUT\n  --keep-outputs        do not delete the shipped outputs before the rerun\n                        (for an entry point that regenerates them in place);\n                        by default they are removed so that only re-creation\n                        counts as reproduction\n  --max-get-gb MAX_GET_GB\n                        skip the up-front content fetch when it would exceed\n                        this (default 5 GiB); a module of a container registry\n                        can be hundreds of GB\n  -o, --output OUTPUT\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
