rts uncertainty. Sign-flip inference assumes exchangeability and a symmetric zero-centered null. The upstream gain modulator was mean-centered and variance-normalized; the supplied copes are not monetary-unit slopes or raw BOLD change. Participant variance maps are absent, so precision-weighted mixed-effects inference is unavailable. These limitations are stated in [the report](/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-ai-research-next/preparation-20261015/cold-stamped-op-judge-target/results/report.md) and [protocol](/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-ai-research-next/preparation-20261015/cold-stamped-op-judge-target/analysis-protocol.md).\n\n## Worker state and access attribution\n\nThe external worker-stop receipt records a successful exit, the requested HEAD \"'`8b5bcdaa999289a47f066ba829511d450301c573`, and an empty worktree/index. That supports worker credit for committing and tracking the delivered files; later coordinator preservation does not add credit. At assessment time the hub URL cloned the parent repository'\"'s \"'`main`, whose published refs did not include the requested study commit. In the local clone, 16 result artifacts were available, but the annex remote returned `not available` for all 54 maps. For access, the intended recipient is a researcher using the authorized Git plus annex route; anonymous access was not required. Required coverage is the exact study commit, locked environment, all 54 input maps, and the outputs/logs needed to inspect and reproduce the report. The tested host was macOS 27 ARM64 in an authorized local context; this does not establish access from another host. Access to part of the content supports `partial` on `must/016`.\n\n## Checklist link and stamp\n\nThe [checklist app URL](2026-10-16-url.txt) opens these answers. The validated canonical record is [response JSON](2026-10-16-response.json); the raw probe output is [probes JSON](2026-10-16-probes.json).\n\nProduced 2026-10-16 by `assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles` 